ding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'>.</li><li style='margin-bottom: 12px;'>• 16. The captain of the team often carries a <span class='question-badge'>16</span> <input type='text' id='ans-16' style='width: 150px; padding: 6px; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 6px; outline: none;'>.</li></ul></div><div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #00cec9; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Questions 17-20</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A, B or C</strong>.</span></div><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;'><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>17</span> 17. Montreal Curling Club is famous as</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-17' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='17'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> the champion club of the local league.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> the oldest sports club in the region.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> the most influential club in winter sports.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>18</span> 18. The Caledonian Curling Club was formed in order to</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-18' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='18'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> attract interest in the sport.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> train young players.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> fix regulations for the game.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>19</span> 19. In the 16th century, curling avoided being banned because</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-19' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='19'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> it was already so popular.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> it was good training for battle.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> it was only played by children.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>20</span> 20. Early curling games in Canada used implements made of</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-20' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='20'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> local material.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> imported stone.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'>